<%- include('../partials/head', { title: 'AI assistant' }) %>
<%- include('../partials/ambient') %><%- include('../partials/topbar') %><%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
<main class="main vp-ai-settings">
  <div class="flex-between" style="flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-bottom:18px"><div><h2 style="font-size:23px;margin:0">AI assistant</h2><p class="muted" style="margin:6px 0 0">Configure your provider, credentials, and assistant tools.</p></div><span id="aiActiveStatus" class="pill pill-gray">Checking connection…</span></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Bring your own API key</div><p class="hint">You supply your own provider API key. The selected provider bills you directly. This panel does not deduct AI credits or charge for model inference. Your provider’s pricing, quotas, and rate limits apply. Provider outages or invalid keys can prevent requests from succeeding.</p><p class="hint">Bring your own API key. No panel-imposed AI usage quotas. Your provider's pricing, quotas, and rate limits apply.</p></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Add provider configuration</div>
    <form id="aiCredentialForm" class="grid grid-2" autocomplete="off">
      <div class="form-group"><label for="aiProvider">Provider</label><select id="aiProvider"><option value="openai">OpenAI</option><option value="anthropic">Anthropic</option><option value="openrouter">OpenRouter</option><option value="compatible">OpenAI-compatible endpoint</option></select></div>
      <div class="form-group"><label for="aiNickname">Nickname (optional)</label><input id="aiNickname" maxlength="60" placeholder="Personal key"/></div>
      <div class="form-group"><label for="aiModel">Model</label><select id="aiModel"></select><input id="aiCustomModel" maxlength="160" placeholder="Model identifier" hidden/><button id="aiLoadModels" type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline" style="margin-top:7px">Refresh models</button><small id="aiModelsStatus" class="hint" aria-live="polite"></small></div>
      <div class="form-group" id="aiEndpointGroup" hidden><label for="aiEndpoint">Compatible API base URL (HTTPS)</label><input id="aiEndpoint" type="url" placeholder="https://api.example.com/v1" autocomplete="url"/><small class="hint">Public HTTPS hostnames only. Local and private network destinations are blocked.</small></div>
      <div class="form-group" style="grid-column:1/-1"><label for="aiApiKey">Provider API key</label><input id="aiApiKey" type="password" minlength="12" maxlength="500" autocomplete="new-password" required placeholder="Paste your provider key"/><small class="hint">The key is encrypted before it is stored. It is never shown again or sent to the browser after saving.</small></div>
      <div style="grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Save configuration</button><span class="status" id="aiFormStatus" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
    </form>
  </div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Saved provider keys</div><div id="aiCredentials"><p class="hint">Loading saved configurations…</p></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Assistant tool permissions</div><p class="hint">Read-only tools access only VMs your account can access. Start, stop, and restart require per-user opt-in and an administrator release switch (<code>AI_VM_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED=1</code>). The switch defaults off; when off, lifecycle tools are rejected server-side even if a saved user preference is enabled. Each action still requires an explicit, target-bound approval. Snapshot creation/restoration, guest files, and guest commands remain unavailable.</p><div id="aiTools"><p class="hint">Loading tools…</p></div><button id="aiSaveTools" type="button" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:14px">Save tool permissions</button><span id="aiToolsStatus" class="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Connection and tool history</div><p class="hint">Provider usage and charges are not estimated by this panel. Usage details are shown only when reliably returned by a provider; no internal token balance or allowance is tracked.</p><div id="aiHistory"><p class="hint">Loading history…</p></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Credential encryption setup</div><p class="hint">The administrator must set <code>AI_CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> to a persistent, secret 32-byte key (base64 or 64-character hex) before credentials can be saved. Generate one with <code>openssl rand -base64 32</code>, place it in the server environment, then restart the panel. Keep a secure backup: losing this key makes saved credentials unrecoverable. Rotate it only through a planned decrypt-and-re-encrypt migration.</p></div>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/music') %><%- include('../partials/foot') %>
<script src="/js/ai-settings.js" defer></script>
